For the panel to actually show a data, you need to put query under the query tab inside panel editor. make sure the query name is exactly as shown in this file.

note : if the query is not returning any value, it will show as a "-" on the value.

Query :
1. CPU Usage :
Query name : usage
Query : sum(rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{container!="", container!="POD"}[5m]))

2. CPU Request :
Query name : request
Query : sum(kube_pod_container_resource_requests{resource="cpu", unit="core"})

3. CPU Limits :
Query name : limits
Query : sum(kube_pod_container_resource_limits{resource="cpu", unit="core"})

4. CPU Capacity :
Query name : capacity
Query : sum(kube_node_status_capacity{resource="cpu"})
